  "body": "See conditions above https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#update-a-style-block. Currently the spec says \"no\".  https://w3c-test.org/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-style-element/style_type_change.html says \"yes\", and passes in Chrome and Firefox. It fails in Edge (verified) and Safari (according to the not-super-reliable wpt.fyi: https://wpt.fyi/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-style-element/style_type_change.html).\r\n\r\nSo we have a 2/2 split, and tests that don't match the spec. What should we do? Maybe ask the CSSWG?",
